---
import Spires from '../components/Spires.astro'
import Transcript from '../components/Transcript.astro'
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import { installPublished, principlesPublished } from '../site'

const runIn = 'font-medium text-ink'
---

<Page
  title="Spyria: a shared workspace for teams and their agents"
  description="A self-hosted workspace where your team and its AI agents share chats, sandboxed runtimes and pull requests. Your keys, your servers, your sign-in."
>
  <section
    aria-labelledby="hero-heading"
    class="grid items-center gap-y-10 pt-12 sm:pt-16 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] lg:gap-x-12"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h1 id="hero-heading" class="display-1">Coding agents are single-player. Your team isn't.</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-8 text-muted">
        Spyria is a self-hosted workspace where people and agents work in the same chats. Everyone can follow an agent's
        work, answer its questions and pick up where a colleague left off.
      </p>
      {
        (installPublished || principlesPublished) && (
          <p class="title mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-3">
            {installPublished && <a href="/install" class="highlight-link">Install on your server</a>}
            {principlesPublished && <a href="/principles" class="highlight-link">Read the principles</a>}
          </p>
        )
      }
    </div>
    <Spires idPrefix="hero-spires" animated class="spires-band h-[min(40vh,20rem)] w-full lg:h-[min(60vh,34rem)]" />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="problem-heading" class="mt-24 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="problem-heading" class="heading-2">Agents are <span class="whitespace-nowrap">single-player</span> today</h2>
    <div class="body mt-8 space-y-6">
      <p>
        Each person has their own chat window, and each laptop runs its own coding agent. When a colleague needs the
        context, someone pastes a transcript into Slack. The agent's questions wait for the one person who started it. API
        keys live in a password manager, and nobody sees the spend until the invoice arrives.
      </p>
      <p>Teams already know how to work together in shared channels. Their agents don't.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="workspace-heading" class="mt-24 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="workspace-heading" class="heading-2">One workspace for people and agents</h2>
    <div class="body mt-8 space-y-6 text-muted">
      <p>
        <strong class={runIn}>Chats and channels.</strong> Projects, channels, threads and agent chats in one sidebar. Start
        an agent from a channel thread, invite a colleague into its chat, or fork it to try another approach.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class={runIn}>Agents in sandboxes.</strong> Each agent chat gets its own runtime container on a machine you
        run. Pi runs there on the prompting member's API key. Claude Code and Codex run on a member's own laptop with their
        own subscription, and the rest of the team can read along.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class={runIn}>Pull requests from a chat.</strong> Attach a chat to a GitHub repository. The agent works on a
        branch in its runtime, the side panel shows files, changes and commits, and the chat owner opens the pull request
        under their own GitHub account.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class={runIn}>Controls for admins.</strong> Single sign-on per workspace, roles, monthly budgets that stop
        spend when they are reached, shared tool connections and an audit log.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="example-heading" class="mt-24">
    <h2 id="example-heading" class="heading-2 max-w-2xl">One chat, two people, one agent</h2>
    <div class="mt-10 grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <Transcript />
      <div
        role="img"
        aria-label="Screenshot of this chat in Spyria, coming soon"
        class="caption hidden aspect-[4/3] place-items-center rounded-xl border border-line px-6 text-center text-muted lg:grid"
      >
        A screenshot of this chat in Spyria will appear here.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="principles-heading" class="mt-24 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="principles-heading" class="heading-2">Built on a few firm choices</h2>
    <ul class="body mt-8 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line text-muted">
      <li class="py-4">
        <strong class={runIn}>Each member's own model key.</strong> Every model call records who prompted it and whose chat
        it ran in.
      </li>
      <li class="py-4">
        <strong class={runIn}>Subscriptions stay on your laptop.</strong> Claude Code and Codex sign-ins never reach the server.
      </li>
      <li class="py-4">
        <strong class={runIn}>GitHub tokens never enter a runtime.</strong> The server pushes the agent's work on the owner's
        behalf.
      </li>
      <li class="py-4"><strong class={runIn}>Budgets stop spend.</strong> They don't just send a warning.</li>
    </ul>
    {
      principlesPublished && (
        <p class="title mt-6">
          <a href="/principles" class="highlight-link">All the principles, and why</a>
        </p>
      )
    }
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="self-hosted-heading" class="mt-24 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="self-hosted-heading" class="heading-2">Runs on your servers</h2>
    <div class="body mt-8 space-y-6">
      <p>
        One Docker Compose file runs Postgres, the server, the sync service and the model gateway. Runtime hosts dial out to
        it, so a VM or a laptop can run agents without opening a port. People sign in through your own identity provider:
        Google Workspace, Microsoft Entra or any OIDC provider.
      </p>
      <p>
        You need a machine with Docker, an HTTPS address and an identity provider.
        {installPublished && <a href="/install" class="highlight-link">Read the install guide</a>}
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="caption mt-8 text-muted">
      Source available under the Business Source License 1.1. Free in production for organizations with up to 10 members;
      each version becomes Apache 2.0 two years after its release.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Spires idPrefix="footer-spires" slot="footer" class="spires-still mt-10 h-32 w-full" />
</Page>
